			<title>Outbursts from a Massive Star</title>
			<link>https://www.nasa.gov/image-detail/a-giant-star-in-a-distant-galaxy-has-been-mysteriously-erupting-for-at-least-15-years-new-data-from-nasas-chandra-explains-what-is-causing-these-huge-outbursts/</link>
			<description>Using Chandra, astronomers have discovered a previously hidden black hole or neutron star companion that is triggering repeated outbursts from a giant, unstable star.</description>
			<enclosure url="https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/at2016blu.jpg" length="7995149" type="image/jpeg" />
